          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gǎnjí is built from gǎn 'to hurry to' and jí 'a gathering'. The second is inherited from Middle Chinese dzip (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'to gather'; no dictionary we use records an older form of gǎn in this sense, so its history is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
