              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "山村 (shāncūn) is built from 山 'a mountain' and 村 (cūn) 'a village', both inherited from Middle Chinese, srean and tshwon (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as a farmstead."
            }
          ]
